- **C9. Secrets, provenance, process, what is left.** (1) gitleaks `/opt/homebrew/bin/gitleaks`: a RANDOM `ghp_`-shaped canary in a scratch repo rc 1 FIRST (typed into no project file), then `f5a27af0..39e51272` (message and diff) rc 0, separate steps in one `bash -c`. (2) Fixtures: list every numeric and string literal the test file adds (the SKUs `PNL-A4-ONE`, `PNL-A4-TWO`, the prices 50 and 60, the device names `SYN-M1`, `SYN-C1`); none has a price meaning; the data is the importer's SYNTHETIC book; real price books are NEVER opened. (3) Provenance (names, card ids, keys, brief numbers, mutant ids in added lines, the commit message, file names; the PR title key = Minor G-8; the body = Note; the commit author line is the machine owner's: say it, do not grade it). (4) Process: nothing of yours running (`ps` by `b715` argv or cwd; stop only your own PIDs); your slot released by MOVE, `ls .tools/ | /usr/bin/grep heavy-slot` shows no holder naming B715; ports 9820-9829 free at start and end; every scratch change restored byte-equal after every restore (`git diff --quiet` rc 0 in `-base`, `-head`, `-merge`, `-mut`); your clone's refs before and after; the shared repo's ref count and objects mtime unchanged by you; no ref on origin, no PR comment, no push, no Jira write, no mail; quote the last 5 heartbeat lines. (5) Jira (GET only, in-process python of your own, credentials by NAME from `4_Credentials/.env`, token never on argv or printed): `project = MPSCALC AND ( key in (MPSCALC-302, MPSCALC-207) )` whole with comments, `project = MPSCALC AND ( updated >= startOfDay() )`, control `project = MPSCALC AND ( text ~ "zzqq7f3anosuchtoken" )` = 0; if not readable, "Jira NOT READ" and NOT RUN. MPSCALC-302 (RELAYED: Backlog, Medium, labels lane-e, tier-1, 0 comments): state its acceptance as Jira holds it and mark MET / PARTLY / NOT MET per clause with `file:line` at the head. (6) Evidence hygiene: 0 non-ASCII bytes in STATUS and evidence (`LC_ALL=C /usr/bin/grep -c '[^ -~]'`; control: a planted raw byte 1), no person's name, no card id, no four-underscore run.

## GRADING (binding; capability decides, a comparison only finds candidates)
- **G-1 delta, sentence and claims.** **Blocker:** a path beyond the two; a byte of the refusal sentence changed; a byte of `docs`, `web`, `.github`, `scripts`, `tools`, another `src` path, an existing test file; a removed or loosened existing line or row beyond the 2 product lines; a test name lost; the head moved; a person's name, real price, BID, SKU, customer name or secret in an added line or commit message. **Major:** a builder claim your measurement contradicts (1 commit, 2 paths, +158 -2, 4 names, the six counts, Import 187, Api 2972); a row that types a sentence the product does not answer; names added other than 4.
- **G-2 kill proof.** **Major of the class:** a named mutant (P1 to P6) NOT red under its credited rows; any variant that lets a count-preserving tamper say AGREE and survives the whole Import suite AND is reachable by a test-only row (Q1 to Q10, the seeded edits, F1 to F8); a row that cannot fail; a row whose expectation is read from the code under test. **Major (not of the class):** a forcing row (F1-F8) the new product answers AGREE to that the OLD product refused (a regression the count test caught). **Minor, one ticket-shaped line each:** an assertion UNPINNED by any mutant whose removal leaves the rows' power unchanged; a survivor that no test-only row can kill and that is equivalent by program (a FACT). A survivor an existing file kills = Note (P6 is this, RELAYED: re-measure). A controls failure (c0/c1/c2 red, c3 red, cw-weak not behaving) = the instrument is broken: re-do, never a finding.
- **G-3 false refusals.** **Blocker:** a legitimate synthetic store the old product agreed on and the new one refuses (L1-L12); a refusal whose number disagrees with the store. A case the importer cannot produce = NOT REACHABLE FROM THE IMPORTER (a FACT, not a pass). Real-book behaviour is NOT TESTED, never "fine".
- **G-4 stability, Linux.** A row that fails or flakes in your runs = Major; a construct that fails on `ubuntu-latest` (PR job log or cited behaviour) = Major; unprovable = UNMEASURED.
- **G-5 CI line.** A warning, a failed or skipped test, or non-zero rc at the combined tree = Blocker; a count contradicting the builder = Major; a red you reproduce 3 of 3 alone = Blocker; a flaky red you cannot reproduce = Note.
- **G-6 CI and CodeQL.** A failing check-run on the head or merge result = Major; an analysis missing (NOT scanned, never clean) = Major; a NEW alert with security severity high or higher or rule severity `error` = Blocker; below both = Minor; a check `in_progress` at the verdict: the line says `CI pending: <names>`, at most GO WITH FOLLOW-UPS (conditional); checks that ran on a merge commit main has since left = a FACT, Note when your C6 on the combined tree is green.
- **G-7 overlap, merge.** A path shared with a live lane or open PR = Major; a conflict marker against current main = Major for the order; a combined tree whose PR blobs differ from the head's = Major. **G-8 hygiene.** A ticket key in a code line, commit message or test name = Major; a key/name/percent in the PR title = Minor (title only matters if the squash subject came from it; for one commit it is the commit title); in the PR body = Note; non-ASCII in added lines = Major; a gitleaks hit = Blocker. **Docs:** a doc line that now understates the check (C5) = Minor.
- **Verdict token.** **GO** needs every check-run at the head completed and green, both CodeQL thresholds met on 4 of 4 analyses, the CI line green at the combined tree, C2 and C3 complete, 0 findings above Note. **GO WITH FOLLOW-UPS** = Minor or Note only. **NO GO** = any Blocker or Major (list each by id with its class for the card). A required check you could not run makes the first and last lines add ` (conditional: <reason>)`; a C2 or C3 that could not be run is always conditional; `CI pending: <names>` is always conditional. **Prediction (the drafter's, to be beaten or confirmed, never copied): GO WITH FOLLOW-UPS. The likely weak spots are Minor: a doc line that says "count", and the P6 credit sitting on an old row. The drafter's open doubt is F4 (a device whose every record is replaced vanishes from `devicesBySheet`); the old product refused it by count and the new product should too, but this is the reading of the source, not a measurement.**

## VERDICT
First line of STATUS: `GATE VERDICT B715: pr118 <GO|GO WITH FOLLOW-UPS|NO GO> round 1 of 2 (NO GO 0 of 2 before this gate) @ 39e5127 (C1 delta <1 commit, 2 paths, +158 -2 y/n> sentence byte-equal <y/n> removed product lines 2 <y/n> existing-test blobs equal <y/n> combined tree = host merge tree <y/n> names lost <n> added <4 y/n> hygiene hits <n> - C2 controls c0 c1 c2 c3 cw-weak <as expected y/n> named mutants P1-P6 <k of 6 red under credited rows> own mutants Q1-Q10 <k killed, k equivalent, k survivors> seeded <k of 3> forcing rows F1-F8 <k refused as predicted> survivors of the whole Import suite <names|none> rows no mutant turns red <n> unpinned assertions <n> - C3 legitimate cases L1-L12 <k agree-unchanged, k not reachable> false refusals <n> real books NOT TESTED - C4 3 runs <green y/n> zone and culture <y/n> Linux log <read|pending|UNMEASURED> - C6 build warnings <n> Engine/Import/Api <e/i/a> failed <n> skipped <n> - C7 checks <n completed of n> pending <names|none> CodeQL analyses <n of 4> open alerts new high+ <n> new error <n> mergeable_state <s> - C8 conflicts <n> overlap <n> main moved <y/n> - C9 gitleaks canary rc <n> scan rc <n> residue <none|named>) majors+: <ids, or none>`. A NO GO line ends with `majors+: B715-n, ...` naming every Major and Blocker by id and its class (for the card). Then the sections as the template's VERDICT list (Step 0 / REFUSE counts / PINS at start, mid, verdict with the merge ref, parents, tree and #117/#112 heads / instrument and load / predictions with evidence paths / C1-C9 / cases and mutant tables / assertion-pin table / forcing-row table / legitimate-case table / check-run table at start and verdict / merge table / findings `B715-n` with severity, `path:line`, instrument, FAIL met, GRADING id, fix-shape in prose, the regression that would be red, evidence class / FOR TUESDAY / ROUND-CAP STATEMENT (both counts above; per finding whether one new commit fixes it and what a round-2 builder kit must hold) / FOUND / TESTED / HOW / NOT TESTED / corrections / processes, slots, trees left / **UNMEASURED** last). **Last line, exactly one of:** `VERDICT: B715 pr118 b711/mps-parity-multiset @ <sha7> <GO|GO WITH FOLLOW-UPS|NO GO> (round 1 of 2; CI <complete|pending: names>) on main <sha7>` (`<sha7>` after `@` = the head you gated; after `main` by `ls-remote` at the verdict; findings with severities on the line above, `B715-1 Minor, ...`; no landing words) or `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY` + ONE question.

## LANDING, MERGE AND HOLD (Tuesday's; you write it into FOR TUESDAY and do none of it)
MPS lands by SQUASH with the head pinned (`1_Project_Definition/CLARIFICATIONS.md:809`: "squash with the head pinned (`--match-head-commit`, the MPS convention, entry 04:52 above)", read the whole line; project `CLAUDE.md:50-52`: the org ruleset requires CodeQL results on `main`; seats push a branch only; Tuesday opens PRs and merges once CodeQL is green). Tuesday runs `gh pr merge 118 -R datasecau/MPS-Commercial-Calculator --squash --match-head-commit 39e51272b6b2733d50764e4277f8f0158e8f0794` after the gate, CodeQL and the checks are green; you never merge, push, comment, mark ready or re-run a check. **NOT deployed:** a merge is not a deploy, MPS hosted is one card per deploy. A GO or GO WITH FOLLOW-UPS: CodeQL and checks green first; the squash text is the commit's own (one commit, subject above); the records seat, not this seat, moves MPSCALC-302 (and MPSCALC-207, which the builder reports still reads Backlog though #84 landed) and ticket-shapes the residue. **The product owner's hand-over (not yours, name it in FOR TUESDAY):** a real-book `prove` run is the only check that touches a real shape, and it stays with the product owner. **A NO GO is not final:** say which finding sits in the one commit, whether ONE new commit on the same branch fixes it, what a round-2 builder kit must hold, and which findings would need no re-gate.

## LOAD (binding; the MPS heavy-slot convention)
8 cores; load1 read 5.4 to 9.2 at drafting. Heavy = `dotnet restore`, `build`, `test` (including `--list-tests` and every mutant build and run), the full CI line, the whole Import and Api projects under a mutant, every scratch-merge build. Git, `gh` GETs and Jira GETs are light. **Start a heavy run only while `uptime` load1 is below 7** at two reads 4 s apart (not independent: say so), recorded beside the result; at 7 or over poll every 20 s and log; do light work meanwhile (C1, predictions, assertion-pin reading, the clone, C7 polling, Jira). **Then take ONE slot atomically:** `mkdir '<project>/.tools/heavy-slot-1' 2>/dev/null || mkdir '<project>/.tools/heavy-slot-2' 2>/dev/null || mkdir '<project>/.tools/heavy-slot-3'`, write `B715 <start> <label>` into its `holder`; read every other holder first (drafter: none held; a holder that looks stale is reported, never removed; a slot directory with no holder file is reported, never taken over). All taken: wait 3 minutes and retry. One slot, one heavy job at a time; re-read load1 at the start of EACH job inside a held slot; for a run longer than a few minutes hold `.tools/b715/heavy.lock` (a directory, pid inside, released by a MOVE). Release ONLY your own slot by a MOVE into `.tools/_quarantine/2026-10-26_B715_<slot>_<label>/`, never `rm`. The shared `.tools/.git-lock` wraps GIT REF WRITES ONLY, never a build or a test. **A MOVING heartbeat** (counter plus `date`) goes to `.tools/b715/logs/heartbeat.txt` every 30 s from every waiter and long job. A wait loop never uses `pgrep -f` or `ps | grep` on a pattern in its own command line (wait on a pid with `kill -0`, `wait $!`, or a done-marker file). Release the slot between the whole-solution runs and the mutant matrix so other seats can take one. NO artificial load. **NuGet homes SEAT-LOCAL**, proven. The Import project is small (187 tests, the builder's whole-project mutant runs are quick); the Api project is the long run (7 to 9 minutes): run it once at `-merge` (C6) and at most once under a mutant.

## HOLDS
- Datasec / MPS Commercial Calculator only. No deploy, `az`, Kudu, Entra, Graph, docker, ssh. **No HTTP to any hosted or production site or app host.** Network: the one explicit-refspec `git fetch` of Step 1 into YOUR clone, `gh api -X GET` under the project `GH_CONFIG_DIR`, Jira GET as C9 allows, the NuGet restore into your seat-local cache. `gh run rerun`, `gh workflow run`, `gh api -X POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE` forbidden. Never dismiss an alert. No decision-queue tool in any form, no scoreboard, no Artifact, Docs, mail, chat or publish tool. No web, node, npm or Playwright.
- **Git in the project repo `2_Project_Files`: READ verbs only** (`--no-optional-locks`: `ls-remote`, `log`, `show`, `diff`, `cat-file`, `ls-tree`, `rev-parse`, `rev-list`, `merge-base`, `grep`, `config --get`, `remote get-url`); `clone --no-hardlinks` FROM it; `fetch`, `worktree add`, `checkout --detach`, legacy `merge-tree`, `merge-tree --write-tree`, scratch `merge`/`branch` only inside `.tools/b715/repo` and `.tools/wt-b715-*`. No git verb in the project root. **Forbidden everywhere:** `merge-tree --write-tree` in the shared repo, `gc`, `worktree prune`, `reset` in the shared repo, `clean`, `stash`, `fetch --prune`, `--shared`, `--reference`.
- **Not yours (never read to obey, edit, quarantine, kill, stop or lock-break):** `b711`, `wt-b711-*` (the builder: its trees, scripts, scratch and `Briefs/2026-10-26_B711_*` evidence are READ-FORBIDDEN for the mutant method; the builder's STATUS is readable; `Briefs/` evidence folders ARE readable for COMPARISON only after your own table is written), `b686`, `wt-b686-*`, `b700`, `wt-b700-*`, `b692`, `wt-b692-*`, `b685`, `b694`, `b654`, `b5*`, `qa-*`, `backup-*`, `_quarantine*`, every other seat's `.tools/b6*` and `.tools/b7*`. Name everything of yours `b715` / `G135`. The shared SDK `.tools/dotnet/` is read-only. Never open the builder's mutator scripts before your own mutant table is written.
- **Real price books are confidential.** Never open `2_Project_Files/.local/`, `1_Project_Definition/Source_Documents/`, `.tools/backup-*`, or any real book or store; every scratch row is synthetic (the importer's own `SyntheticBooks` variants). Secrets only as environment. Never open `4_Credentials/.env` except by NAME for the Jira GET.
- **Never delete** (`rm`, `git branch -D`): quarantine to `.tools/b715/quarantine/`. **Never `cd`**; absolute single-quoted paths (they contain a space and `!`); `bash -c '...'` or a QUOTED heredoc where a path with spaces is in command position; quote URLs holding `?`; no unquoted word starting with `=` (use `----`); bash, not zsh, for loops; `/usr/bin/grep -i` with a positive control for every count (`-E`, no `-P`); `python3 -I` for anything reading a file you did not write; write `${VAR}:path`, never `$VAR:path`. Never kill a process by basename. No person's name in any id, file, branch or STATUS (say "the product owner"), no decision-card id.
- **RESUME (at about 80% of context, or at the hard stop):** stop new checks, write STATUS sections `PROGRESS` and `RESUME` (each check done/partial/not started with evidence paths, the exact next commands, the state of every scratch tree and mutant with its restore proof, the slot, the pins, the predictions file, the seeds), restore every mutant, release the slot, end `STOPPED: NEEDS TUESDAY` + "continue in a fresh seat from RESUME?". A conditional verdict with the open instances listed beats a RESUME with nothing shippable; a verdict that did not finish C2 or C3 is conditional at best.
- **STANDING LINES.** PRIOR-WORK CHECK: a builder READY without a PRIOR WORK section is returned. No message to any human. No Jira write (reads only, C9). Never delete (quarantine). Findings only.

## NOT TESTED BY DESIGN (state each unless you do better)
The hosted site and any signed-in browser; the CI Linux runner beyond the PR job logs and documented behaviour; a Windows file system; the `web` and `python` jobs (no path of theirs in the diff); real deals, real price books and a real-store `prove` run (the product owner's); any run under artificial load; the builder's scripts (you rebuild yours); other lanes beyond the path intersection and scratch merges; PRs #112 and #117 themselves; the importer's panel READER beyond what the synthetic books drive (not changed here); the Api project's behaviour beyond one unchanged whole run; any behaviour change or new word.
